# What must never reach a build context.
#
# Every Dockerfile here copies what it needs by name, so this file is not about trimming the
# context for speed. It is about the three things that would change what gets built or what ships:
# a local build's output landing on top of the container's own, a secret arriving as a file, and
# the repository's history riding along inside an image that has no use for it.
#
# web/admin matters most: the API image copies that whole directory, and a local node_modules would
# overwrite the one `bun install` just produced inside the image, for a different platform.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/bin
**/obj
**/.vite
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.vs
.vscode
.idea

# Secrets, in every shape .gitignore already refuses.
**/.env
**/*.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json

# Local data volumes, if anybody has run the stack from a checkout.
.data/
.minio/
